{"id": "EUVD-2026-59117", "enisaUuid": "abbbdd8b-716b-369d-8ff6-844ea522e185", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\ndibs: loopback: validate offset and size in move_data()\n\nThe loopback move_data() performs a memcpy into the registered DMB\nwithout checking whether offset + size exceeds the DMB length.  Unlike\nreal ISM hardware, which enforces memory region bounds natively, the\nsoftware loopback has no such protection.\n\nA peer-supplied out-of-bounds offset or oversized write would result in\nan OOB write past the allocated kernel buffer.  Add an explicit bounds\ncheck before the memcpy to reject such requests with -EINVAL.", "datePublished": "2026-08-15T05:51:45", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-16T18:42:39", "baseScore": 7.8, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:L/AC:L/PR:L/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H", "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/ee188a6b264b71315a67f1b9470faad308b730d2", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/b2f426a9a22886071966432ede8fceafffe12b8c", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/94fe0ab01b480b52bd8f977edbd845ef375d69fd", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/78237e3c0720fcc6eb9b87e90fd70f63eeca886f"], "aliases": ["GHSA-96mx-hwj9-j649", "CVE-2026-72018"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.17, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "11d26402-2478-30db-a367-a48937e2e186", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.1.5"}, {"id": "5f49758a-6e1c-3574-a0d2-c97022d4db07", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "f7a22071dbf316c982fb44308874bd7ad9ac2091 <b2f426a9a22886071966432ede8fceafffe12b8c"}, {"id": "752b3ecf-9e91-36c9-ae61-c85602198f69", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.40"}, {"id": "84df9c98-be7d-3563-89ff-38b283f68a18", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "f7a22071dbf316c982fb44308874bd7ad9ac2091 <78237e3c0720fcc6eb9b87e90fd70f63eeca886f"}, {"id": "bca528a2-f5ba-3d70-8259-2e8199f6d476", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.10"}, {"id": "be90518e-e61a-3fbb-bb18-e7b85c0f5d41", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2"}, {"id": "c9175ed8-feee-3419-91a1-8ef25ed571a9", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "f7a22071dbf316c982fb44308874bd7ad9ac2091 <94fe0ab01b480b52bd8f977edbd845ef375d69fd"}, {"id": "cfb37548-2a6e-38ff-afff-672bda67b18b", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "f1c7565c-c856-309b-a5d4-b7a46b82dddb", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.97"}, {"id": "f5a005d9-c7ec-3bfb-ac08-33d2b3c2242f", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "f7a22071dbf316c982fb44308874bd7ad9ac2091 <ee188a6b264b71315a67f1b9470faad308b730d2"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "2ff20bb4-7b89-394a-9c0e-07757fe49c5a", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}], "isExploited": false}